{"parentUuid":"e6a62608-5c5d-4666-879d-57dfd0f052e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgniAZ8pLJzAKvD3tbNRC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":136846,"output_tokens":1771,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":447},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2300,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1771,"cache_read_input_tokens":136846,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2300},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12152,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"70dd786a-7bd9-404e-984f-95d00b021814","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgniAYpyJA5QPL4jfMaMB","requestRef":"be10b444-d1d4-4e3d-9d12-004ee252d0bc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"3579f325-ecd1-4221-9466-fbaa39e1b324","timestamp":"2026-11-07T01:36:39.107Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/viewer-objects","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"3579f325-ecd1-4221-9466-fbaa39e1b324","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgniAZ8pLJzAKvD3tbNRC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The floor map and routing now work on your splat, and P-005 has a candidate, obj-0048, which still needs a person to confirm it.** The work is committed and pushed to draft PR #3. Lint and tests pass (99 passed, 2 skipped); I ran pytest directly without torch rather than `make check`, and haven't looked at CI for this push.\n\n## Floor map\nSwitching to your splat broke the floor map: connected floor at 0.6 m wide fell to 0.2 m², so routing was unusable. Floaters were marking the real aisle as blocked, including 35% of the path the camera took.\n\n| Connected floor | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.3 m wide | 1.2 m² | 15.0 m² |\n| 0.6 m wide (person) | 0.2 m² | 6.6 m² |\n| 0.8 m wide | 0 m² | 1.1 m² |\n\n- **The fix:** if a camera ray passes through a spot to reach a surface behind it, that spot must be empty, so any splats there are floaters. This removed 190,844 of them (`app/nav/carve.py`). Keeping a person's width clear along the camera path then joins the aisle into a full loop around the equipment.\n- **Scale:** the camera stays 1.28–1.40 m above the floor, which supports the scene being in metres but doesn't prove it.\n\n## P-005\n- **Candidate:** obj-0048 is one of two matching black inline pumps on a plinth, possibly a duty and standby pair. It's the best fit for a critical process pump.\n- **How it's recorded:** `manual_visual_unconfirmed`, confidence 0.3 (my own estimate), because no tag is readable. The mapping is only in a local test file so far, not in the commit.\n- **Route:** 6.8 m long for a person, stopping 0.8 m from the pump. Seven rendered views along it show no clipping through walls or equipment, checked by eye.\n- **Viewing point:** the view at the stop is poor because the video never saw the pump that close, while 2 m back looks demo-ready. Routes now also return that point as `view_from`.\n\n## Still weak\n- **Wide routes:** the `carrying` profile gets a 409 error from this start point, because too little floor is that wide. The person and robot profiles both work.\n- **Viewer:** it doesn't draw routes yet, and navigation is 25% of the score. That's the biggest demo gap, and it's in Benjamin's area.\n- **Labels:** most objects on the new scene are `unsure` or `unknown`, and many of Qwen's pump labels are wrong. The earlier AI review needs redoing for this scene.\n- **Scene comparison:** Valmet's scene reaches 7.4 m² connected at 0.6 m, slightly more than ours, but without carving, so the two aren't directly comparable. Your splat's main advantage is that it looks much better.\n\n## Questions for you\n1. **Is obj-0048 the right pump, or is it the one in front of it?** Someone needs to check this, ideally with Valmet's engineer. The front pump is more visible but is merged into obj-0001 with its pipes, so I'd have to split it out.\n2. **Was the video filmed by someone walking through the room?** I assumed so when keeping the camera path clear. If it's a rendered fly-through, that corridor isn't proof of free floor, and I'd rerun without it.\n3. **Can I publish a `scene-v2` Release to the private repo?** Benjamin needs the new scene to test, and it's derived from Valmet's video, so I'm checking first. I recommend yes, deleting it before the repo goes public as with the earlier Releases.\n4. **Should Eduard's PR #2 go in first?** I recommend merging it, then rebasing PR #3 on top, since both add A*. His version would then gain footprints, stop distance and refusal reasons from mine.\n\nOnce those are settled, I'd add route drawing to the viewer next, if Benjamin isn't already on it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":136846,"output_tokens":1771,"outpu