{"parentUuid":"ab343742-78a8-4d76-95e5-62465488c58e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgniyWoynyb9CKe5qH9u2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, nothing new is merged. `main` is still at Eduard's PR #1 (`a10ea67`), so it has none of the work from this session.\n\n| PR | Status | Contents |\n|---|---|---|\n| #1 Eduard | Merged | Backend API and first floor map |\n| #2 Eduard | Open | A* routing with body sizes |\n| #3 Mine | Open draft, 12 commits ahead of `main` | Viewer objects, real routing, floor fix, `view_from`, `make scene` |\n\nUntil #3 is merged, teammates on `main` don't have `make scene` or the floor fix.\n\nGitHub reports no conflict for either PR on its own, but that only compares each one against the current `main`. Both add A* to `app/nav/route.py`, so merging one will probably make the other conflict.\n\nMy recommended order:\n1. Merge #2, so Eduard's work goes in as his.\n2. Rebase #3 on top, keeping footprints, stop distance, refusal reasons and `view_from`, and run the tests.\n3. Mark #3 ready and merge it once CI passes.\n\nOne catch is that PR #3 is based on `benjamin/webviewer`, so merging it also brings Benjamin's viewer work into `main`. It's worth telling him first.\n\nDo you want me to go ahead with this order? Merging is your call because `main` is what you demo, and #2 is Eduard's PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":519,"cache_read_input_tokens":151829,"output_tokens":461,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":519,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":461,"cache_read_input_tokens":151829,"cache_creation_input_tokens":519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_