{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01W2z6u48mE7ruGEe22DNPVT","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"eb1ff47f-cfbf-49b1-a15e-4ca693f2c22a","ownerOrganizationUuid":"af454b37-7570-4ffb-9890-36a908611f8b"}
{"parentUuid":"bf420953-526b-4a53-9735-c6f971077178","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dcbd8ba1-3522-4096-ad5e-41a09d6240dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013mABkyccdxmWWsck9rNeF3","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Routes on the floor map: A* for a body size, to free floor beside an object.\n\nA body fits a cell if its clearance is at least the body's radius. Positions are in the scene's\ncoordinates, and paths stay on the floor.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport heapq\nimport math\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nPoint = tuple[float, float, float]\n# Width in metres, and whether it can pass under overhead obstacles.\nPROFILES = {\"robot\": (0.3, True), \"person\": (0.6, False), \"carrying\": (1.0, False)}\nREACH = 0.8  # how far from an object's box a person can stop and still service it\nSTEPS = [(a, b, math.hypot(a, b)) for a in (-1, 0, 1) for b in (-1, 0, 1) if a or b]\n\n\nclass NoRoute(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"No path exists. The message says why, for showing to the user.\"\"\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass FloorMap:\n    origin: np.ndarray\n    cell: float\n    floor_height: float\n    up: np.ndarray\n    axes: tuple[int, int]\n    clearance: np.ndarray\n    clearance_low: np.ndarray\n\n    @classmethod\n    def load(cls, path: Path | str) -> \"FloorMap\":\n        with np.load(path) as data:\n            return cls(\n                origin=data[\"origin\"],\n                cell=float(data[\"cell\"]),\n                floor_height=float(data[\"floor_height\"]),\n                up=data[\"up\"],\n                axes=tuple(int(a) for a in data[\"axes\"]),\n                clearance=data[\"clearance\"],\n                clearance_low=data[\"clearance_low\"],\n            )\n\n    def to_cell(self, point: Point | list[float]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        flat = np.asarray(point, dtype=float)[list(self.axes)]\n        return tuple(np.floor((flat - self.origin) / self.cell).astype(int).tolist())\n\n    def to_world(self, cell: tuple[int, int]) -> Point:\n        point = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n        for axis, index, low in zip(self.axes, cell, self.origin, strict=True):\n            point[axis] = round(float(low + (index + 0.5) * self.cell), 3)\n        up_axis = 3 - sum(self.axes)\n        point[up_axis] = round(float(self.floor_height / self.up[up_axis]), 3)\n        return tuple(point)\n\n    def fits(self, profile: str, blocked: np.ndarray | None = None) -> np.ndarray:\n        width, low = PROFILES[profile]\n        fits = (self.clearance_low if low else self.clearance) >= width / 2\n        return fits & ~blocked if blocked is not None else fits\n\n    def goal_cells(self, bbox_min: list[float], bbox_max: list[float]) -> np.ndarray:\n        \"\"\"True for cells within reach of an object's box on the floor.\"\"\"\n        rows, cols = np.ogrid[: self.clearance.shape[0], : self.clearance.shape[1]]\n        low = np.asarray(bbox_min, dtype=float)[list(self.axes)]\n        high = np.asarray(bbox_max, dtype=float)[list(self.axes)]\n        x = self.origin[0] + (rows + 0.5) * self.cell\n        y = self.origin[1] + (cols + 0.5) * self.cell\n        gap_x = np.maximum(np.maximum(low[0] - x, x - high[0]), 0)\n        gap_y = np.maximum(np.maximum(low[1] - y, y - high[1]), 0)\n        return np.hypot(gap_x, gap_y) <= REACH\n\n\ndef nearest_fit(fits: np.ndarray, cell: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    free = np.argwhere(fits)\n    if not len(free):\n        return None\n    return tuple(free[np.argmin(((free - cell) ** 2).sum(axis=1))].tolist())\n\n\ndef astar(fits: np.ndarray, start: tuple[int, int], goals: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Shortest path from start to any goal cell, in cells. Empty if there's none.\n\n    Diagonal steps can't cut a corner. The search spreads evenly because goals can be many cells.\n    \"\"\"\n    goal_list = np.argwhere(goals & fits)\n    if not len(goal_list):\n        return []\n    center = goal_list.mean(axis=0)\n    spread = float(np.hypot(*(goal_list - center).T).max())\n\n    def estimate(cell: tuple[int, int]) -> float:\n        return max(math.hypot(cell[0] - center[0], cell[1] - center[1]) - spread, 0.0)\n\n    rows, cols = fits.shape\n    best = {start: 0.0}\n    came: dict[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] = {}\n    heap = [(estimate(start), start)]\n    while heap:\n        _, current = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        if goals[current]:\n            path = [current]\n            while path[-1] in came:\n                path.append(came[path[-1]])\n            return path[::-1]\n        for dr, dc, cost in STEPS:\n            r, c = current[0] + dr, current[1] + dc\n            if not (0 <= r < rows and 0 <= c < cols and fits[r, c]):\n                continue\n            if (\n                dr\n                and dc\n                and not (fits[current[0] + dr, current[1]] and fits[current[0], current[1] + dc])\n            ):\n                continue\n            total = best[current] + cost\n            if total < best.get((r, c), math.inf):\n                best[(r, c)] = total\n                came[(r, c)] = current\n                heapq.heappush(heap, (total + estimate((r, c)), (r, c)))\n    return []\n\n\ndef simplify(path: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Keep only the cells where direction changes.\"\"\"\n    kept = path[:1]\n    for before, here, after in zip(path, path[1:], path[2:], strict=False):\n        if (here[0] - before[0], here[1] - before[1]) != (after[0] - here[0], after[1] - here[1]):\n            kept.append(here)\n    return kept + path[-1:] if len(path) > 1 else kept\n\n\ndef plan_route(\n    floor: FloorMap,\n    start: Point | list[float],\n    bbox_min: list[float],\n    bbox_max: list[float],\n    profile: str = \"person\",\n    blocked: np.ndarray | None = None,\n) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Route to free floor beside an object. Raises NoRoute if the body can't get there.\"\"\"\n    fits = floor.fits(profile, blocked)\n    width = PROFILES[profile][0]\n    begin = nearest_fit(fits, floor.to_cell(start))\n    if begin is None:\n        raise NoRoute(f\"No floor is wide enough for a {width} m body.\")\n    goals = floor.goal_cells(bbox_min, bbox_max)\n    if not (goals & fits).any():\n        raise NoRoute(f\"No free floor beside this object for a {width} m body.\")\n    path = astar(fits, begin, goals)\n    if not path:\n        raise NoRoute(f\"No connected route to this object for a {width} m body.\")\n    length = sum(math.dist(a, b) for a, b in zip(path, path[1:], strict=False)) * floor.cell\n    return {\n        \"path\": [floor.to_world(cell) for cell in simplify(path)],\n        \"length\": round(length, 3),\n        \"profile\": profile,\n        \"width\": width,\n        \"start_moved\": round(math.dist(begin, floor.to_cell(start)) * floor.cell, 3),\n        \"placeholder\": False,\n    }\n\n\ndef placeholder_route(start: Point, goal: Point, floor_y: float) -> tuple[list[Point], float]:\n    \"\"\"Return an L-shaped path on the floor. It ignores obstacles, so it isn't a real route.\"\"\"\n    a = (start[0], floor_y, start[2])\n    corner = (goal[0], floor_y, start[2])\n    b = (goal[0], floor_y, goal[2])\n    path = [a, corner, b]\n    return path, sum(math.dist(p, q) for p, q in zip(path, path[1:], strict=False))\n=====API\nfrom app.api.store import ChangeError, SceneStore\nfrom app.nav.route import FloorMap, NoRoute, placeholder_route, plan_route\n\nDEFAULT_ASSETS = Path(\"fixtures/sample_assets.json\")\nPosition = Annotated[list[float], Field(min_length=3, max_length=3)]\nDEFAULT_FLOOR = Path(\"data/scene/equipment_room/nav_grid.npz\")\n\n\nclass RouteRequest(BaseModel):\n    start: Position\n    object_id: str\n    profile: Literal[\"robot\", \"person\", \"carrying\"] = \"person\"\n\n\nclass ChangeRequest(BaseModel):\n    op: Literal[\"add\", \"move\", \"remove\"]\n        x: float, y: float, z: float, radius: Annotated[float, Query(gt=0, le=100)] = 3.0\n    ) -> dict:\n        return {\"assets\": store.nearby((x, y, z), radius)}\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/route\")\n    def route(request: RouteRequest) -> dict:\n        asset = require(request.object_id)\n        if floor is not None:\n            try:\n                return plan_route(\n                    floor, request.start, asset[\"bbox_min\"], asset[\"bbox_max\"], request.profile\n                )\n            except NoRoute as error:\n                raise HTTPException(409, str(error)) from None\n        floor_y = store.scene.get(\"floor_y\", request.start[1])\n        path, length = placeholder_route(tuple(request.start), tuple(asset[\"center\"]), floor_y)\n        return {\n            \"path\": path,\n            \"length\": round(length, 3),\n            \"profile\": request.profile,\n            \"placeholder\": True,\n        }\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/copilot/query\")\n    def copilot(request: CopilotRequest) -> dict:\n        if request.object_id:\n            require(request.object_id)\n        return {\n            \"answer\": \"The copilot isn't connected yet.\",\n            \"observations\": [],\n            \"hypotheses\": [],\n            \"citations\": [],\n            \"confidence\": 0.0,\n            \"actions\": [],\n            \"placeholder\": True,\n        }\n=====TESTS\n1:import pytest\n6:from scipy import ndimage  # noqa: E402\n8:from app.nav.route import FloorMap, NoRoute, astar, plan_route  # noqa: E402\n11:def floor_with_wall(gap_cells):\n32:def test_route_goes_through_gap_and_stays_clear():\n48:def test_route_ends_within_reach_of_object():\n54:def test_body_size_decides_who_fits():\n61:def test_blocked_cells_close_the_route():\ndiff --git a/tests/test_api.py b/tests/test_api.py\nindex a550f0d..11a0a93 100644\n--- a/tests/test_api.py\n+++ b/tests/test_api.py\n@@ -51,6 +51,29 @@ def test_route_is_marked_placeholder(client):\n     assert body[\"length\"] == 9\n \n \n+def test_route_uses_floor_map_when_present(tmp_path):\n+    np = pytest.importorskip(\"numpy\")\n+    floor = tmp_path / \"nav_grid.npz\"\n+    open_floor = np.full((200, 200), 2.0, dtype=np.float32)\n+    np.savez(\n+        floor,\n+        origin=np.array([-1.0, -5.0]),\n+        cell=0.05,\n+        floor_height=-1.25,\n+        up=np.array([0.0, -1.0, 0.0]),\n+        axes=np.array([0, 2]),\n+        free=open_floor > 0,\n+        clearance=open_floor,\n+        clearance_low=open_floor,\n+    )\n+    path = tmp_path / \"assets.json\"\n+    path.write_text(json.dumps({\"scene_id\": \"t\", \"assets\": [box(\"far\", [7, 1, 0], \"fixed\")]}))\n+    client = TestClient(create_app(path, floor))\n+    body = client.post(\"/api/route\", json={\"start\": [0, 1.25, 0], \"object_id\": \"far\"}).json()\n+    assert body[\"placeholder\"] is False\n+    assert body[\"path\"][0][1] == 1.25\n+\n+\n def test_move_updates_box_and_is_logged(client):\n     moved = {\"op\": \"move\", \"object_id\": \"near\", \"position\": [5, 1, 0]}\n     assert client.post(\"/api/changes\", json=moved).status_code == 200\n====HEAD\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/route\")\n    def route(request: RouteRequest) -> dict:\n        asset = require(request.object_id)\n        if grid is not None:\n            try:\n                found = plan_route(\n                    grid,\n                    tuple(request.start),\n                    tuple(asset[\"bbox_min\"]),\n                    tuple(asset[\"bbox_max\"]),\n                    width=PROFILES[request.profile],\n                    footprints=footprints(store, request.object_id),\n                )\n            except NoRoute as reason:\n                raise HTTPException(409, str(reason)) from None\n            return {\n                \"path\": found.path,\n                \"length\": round(found.length, 3),\n                \"stop_distance\": round(found.stop_distance, 3),\n                \"view_from\": list(found.view_from),\n                \"profile\": request.profile,\n                \"width\": PROFILES[request.profile],\n                \"placeholder\": False,\n            }\n        floor_y = store.scene.get(\"floor_y\", request.start[1])\n        path, length = placeholder_route(tuple(request.start), tuple(asset[\"center\"]), floor_y)\n        return {\n            \"path\": path,\n            \"length\": round(length, 3),\n            \"profile\": request.profile,\n            \"width\": PROFILES[request.profile],\n            \"placeholder\": True,\n        }\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/copilot/query\")\n12:def room():\n26:def cells_of(route):\n30:def crosses_wall(route, grid=GRID):\n40:def test_route_goes_through_the_gap_and_not_the_wall():\n47:def test_route_stays_on_the_floor_and_stops_close_to_the_target():\n53:def test_too_wide_a_body_gets_a_reason_instead_of_a_route():\n58:def test_footprint_in_the_gap_blocks_then_moving_it_reopens_the_route():\n66:def test_start_inside_an_obstacle_snaps_to_nearby_floor():\n71:def test_start_far_from_any_floor_is_refused():\n76:def test_line_check_sees_blocked_cells():\n83:def test_viewing_point_stands_back_from_the_target_along_the_route():\n# eduard-rednic: eduard\n**Goal:** floor, routing, nearby search and backend API (`app/nav/`, `app/api/`), per docs/PLAN.md.\n**Done:** `make api` on port 8001. PR #1 merged. PR #2 adds real A* with body sizes in `/api/route`, used when `NAV_GRID` or the default `nav_grid.npz` exists; otherwise the marked placeholder.\n**Verified:** `make check` passes. A* takes under 20 ms on the real map. Not yet run against real objects; floor not checked against views.\n**Next:** load `assets_final.json`, pick a reachable `P-005`; object footprints for moves; TimescaleDB.\n**Decided:** no cloud: TimescaleDB runs on the local 5090, and tablets talk only to it.\n**Blockers:** `assets_final.json` and the `P-005` choice from Viktor; Hannu's code isn't on main and his fixture format differs.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8e7fd459-7a82-43cd-9c46-2a1f82bb780c","timestamp":"2026-11-07T01:48:05.189Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Routes on the floor map: A* for a body size, to free floor beside an object.\n\nA body fits a cell if its clearance is at least the body's radius. Positions are in the scene's\ncoordinates, and paths stay on the floor.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport heapq\nimport math\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nPoint = tuple[float, float, float]\n# Width in metres, and whether it can pass under overhead obstacles.\nPROFILES = {\"robot\": (0.3, True), \"person\": (0.6, False), \"carrying\": (1.0, False)}\nREACH = 0.8  # how far from an object's box a person can stop and still service it\nSTEPS = [(a, b, math.hypot(a, b)) for a in (-1, 0, 1) for b in (-1, 0, 1) if a or b]\n\n\nclass NoRoute(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"No path exists. The message says why, for showing to the user.\"\"\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass FloorMap:\n    origin: np.ndarray\n    cell: float\n    floor_height: float\n    up: np.ndarray\n    axes: tuple[int, int]\n    clearance: np.ndarray\n    clearance_low: np.ndarray\n\n    @classmethod\n    def load(cls, path: Path | str) -> \"FloorMap\":\n        with np.load(path) as data:\n            return cls(\n                origin=data[\"origin\"],\n                cell=float(data[\"cell\"]),\n                floor_height=float(data[\"floor_height\"]),\n                up=data[\"up\"],\n                axes=tuple(int(a) for a in data[\"axes\"]),\n                clearance=data[\"clearance\"],\n                clearance_low=data[\"clearance_low\"],\n            )\n\n    def to_cell(self, point: Point | list[float]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        flat = np.asarray(point, dtype=float)[list(self.axes)]\n        return tuple(np.floor((flat - self.origin) / self.cell).astype(int).tolist())\n\n    def to_world(self, cell: tuple[int, int]) -> Point:\n        point = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n        for axis, index, low in zip(self.axes, cell, self.origin, strict=True):\n            point[axis] = round(float(low + (index + 0.5) * self.cell), 3)\n        up_axis = 3 - sum(self.axes)\n        point[up_axis] = round(float(self.floor_height / self.up[up_axis]), 3)\n        return tuple(point)\n\n    def fits(self, profile: str, blocked: np.ndarray | None = None) -> np.ndarray:\n        width, low = PROFILES[profile]\n        fits = (self.clearance_low if low else self.clearance) >= width / 2\n        return fits & ~blocked if blocked is not None else fits\n\n    def goal_cells(self, bbox_min: list[float], bbox_max: list[float]) -> np.ndarray:\n        \"\"\"True for cells within reach of an object's box on the floor.\"\"\"\n        rows, cols = np.ogrid[: self.clearance.shape[0], : self.clearance.shape[1]]\n        low = np.asarray(bbox_min, dtype=float)[list(self.axes)]\n        high = np.asarray(bbox_max, dtype=float)[list(self.axes)]\n        x = self.origin[0] + (rows + 0.5) * self.cell\n        y = self.origin[1] + (cols + 0.5) * self.cell\n        gap_x = np.maximum(np.maximum(low[0] - x, x - high[0]), 0)\n        gap_y = np.maximum(np.maximum(low[1] - y, y - high[1]), 0)\n        return np.hypot(gap_x, gap_y) <= REACH\n\n\ndef nearest_fit(fits: np.ndarray, cell: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    free = np.argwhere(fits)\n    if not len(free):\n        return None\n    return tuple(free[np.argmin(((free - cell) ** 2).sum(axis=1))].tolist())\n\n\ndef astar(fits: np.ndarray, start: tuple[int, int], goals: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Shortest path from start to any goal cell, in cells. Empty if there's none.\n\n    Diagonal steps can't cut a corner. The search spreads evenly because goals can be many cells.\n    \"\"\"\n    goal_list = np.argwhere(goals & fits)\n    if not len(goal_list):\n        return []\n    center = goal_list.mean(axis=0)\n    spread = float(np.hypot(*(goal_list - center).T).max())\n\n    def estimate(cell: tuple[int, int]) -> float:\n        return max(math.hypot(cell[0] - center[0], cell[1] - center[1]) - spread, 0.0)\n\n    rows, cols = fits.shape\n    best = {start: 0.0}\n    came: dict[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] = {}\n    heap = [(estimate(start), start)]\n    while heap:\n        _, current = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        if goals[current]:\n            path = [current]\n            while path[-1] in came:\n                path.append(came[path[-1]])\n            return path[::-1]\n        for dr, dc, cost in STEPS:\n            r, c = current[0] + dr, current[1] + dc\n            if not (0 <= r < rows and 0 <= c < cols and fits[r, c]):\n                continue\n            if (\n                dr\n                and dc\n                and not (fits[current[0] + dr, current[1]] and fits[current[0], current[1] + dc])\n            ):\n                continue\n            total = best[current] + cost\n            if total < best.get((r, c), math.inf):\n                best[(r, c)] = total\n                came[(r, c)] = current\n                heapq.heappush(heap, (total + estimate((r, c)), (r, c)))\n    return []\n\n\ndef simplify(path: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Keep only the cells where direction changes.\"\"\"\n    kept = path[:1]\n    for before, here, after in zip(path, path[1:], path[2:], strict=False):\n        if (here[0] - before[0], here[1] - before[1]) != (after[0] - here[0], after[1] - here[1]):\n            kept.append(here)\n    return kept + path[-1:] if len(path) > 1 else kept\n\n\ndef plan_route(\n    floor: FloorMap,\n    start: Point | list[float],\n    bbox_min: list[float],\n    bbox_max: list[float],\n    profile: str = \"person\",\n    blocked: np.ndarray | None = None,\n) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Route to free floor beside an object. Raises NoRoute if the body can't get there.\"\"\"\n    fits = floor.fits(profile, blocked)\n    width = PROFILES[profile][0]\n    begin = nearest_fit(fits, floor.to_cell(start))\n    if begin is None:\n        raise NoRoute(f\"No floor is wide enough for a {width} m body.\")\n    goals = floor.goal_cells(bbox_min, bbox_max)\n    if not (goals & fits).any():\n        raise NoRoute(f\"No free floor beside this object for a {width} m body.\")\n    path = astar(fits, begin, goals)\n    if not path:\n        raise NoRoute(f\"No connected route to this object for a {width} m body.\")\n    length = sum(math.dist(a, b) for a, b in zip(path, path[1:], strict=False)) * floor.cell\n    return {\n        \"path\": [floor.to_world(cell) for cell in simplify(path)],\n        \"length\": round(length, 3),\n        \"profile\": profile,\n        \"width\": width,\n        \"start_moved\": round(math.dist(begin, floor.to_cell(start)) * floor.cell, 3),\n        \"placeholder\": False,\n    }\n\n\ndef placeholder_route(start: Point, goal: Point, floor_y: float) -> tuple[list[Point], float]:\n    \"\"\"Return an L-shaped path on the floor. It ignores obstacles, so it isn't a real route.\"\"\"\n    a = (start[0], floor_y, start[2])\n    corner = (goal[0], floor_y, start[2])\n    b = (goal[0], floor_y, goal[2])\n    path = [a, corner, b]\n    return path, sum(math.dist(p, q) for p, q in zip(path, path[1:], strict=False))\n=====API\nfrom app.api.store import ChangeError, SceneStore\nfrom app.nav.route import FloorMap, NoRoute, placeholder_route, plan_route\n\nDEFAULT_ASSETS = Path(\"fixtures/sample_assets.json\")\nPosition = Annotated[list[float], Field(min_length=3, max_length=3)]\nDEFAULT_FLOOR = Path(\"data/scene/equipment_room/nav_grid.npz\")\n\n\nclass RouteRequest(BaseModel):\n    start: Position\n    object_id: str\n    profile: Literal[\"robot\", \"person\", \"carrying\"] = \"person\"\n\n\nclass ChangeRequest(BaseModel):\n    op: Literal[\"add\", \"move\", \"remove\"]\n        x: float, y: float, z: float, radius: Annotated[float, Query(gt=0, le=100)] = 3.0\n    ) -> dict:\n        return {\"assets\": store.nearby((x, y, z), radius)}\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/route\")\n    def route(request: RouteRequest) -> dict:\n        asset = require(request.object_id)\n        if floor is not None:\n            try:\n                return plan_route(\n                    floor, request.start, asset[\"bbox_min\"], asset[\"bbox_max\"], request.profile\n                )\n            except NoRoute as error:\n                raise HTTPException(409, str(error)) from None\n        floor_y = store.scene.get(\"floor_y\", request.start[1])\n        path, length = placeholder_route(tuple(request.start), tuple(asset[\"center\"]), floor_y)\n        return {\n            \"path\": path,\n            \"length\": round(length, 3),\n            \"profile\": request.profile,\n            \"placeholder\": True,\n        }\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/copilot/query\")\n    def copilot(request: CopilotRequest) -> dict:\n        if request.object_id:\n            require(request.object_id)\n        return {\n            \"answer\": \"The copilot isn't connected yet.\",\n            \"observations\": [],\n            \"hypotheses\": [],\n            \"citations\": [],\n            \"confidence\": 0.0,\n            \"actions\": [],\n            \"placeholder\": True,\n        }\n=====TESTS\n1:import pytest\n6:from scipy import ndimage  # noqa: E402\n8:from app.nav.route import FloorMap, NoRoute, astar, plan_route  # noqa: E402\n11:def floor_with_wall(gap_cells):\n32:def test_route_goes_through_gap_and_stays_clear():\n48:def test_route_ends_within_reach_of_object():\n54:def test_body_size_decides_who_fits():\n61:def test_blocked_cells_close_the_route():\ndiff --git a/tests/test_api.py b/tests/test_api.py\nindex a550f0d..11a0a93 100644\n--- a/tests/test_api.py\n+++ b/tests/test_api.py\n@@ -51,6 +51,29 @@ def test_route_is_marked_placeholder(client):\n     assert body[\"length\"] == 9\n \n \n+def test_route_uses_floor_map_when_present(tmp_path):\n+    np = pytest.importorskip(\"numpy\")\n+    floor = tmp_path / \"nav_grid.npz\"\n+    open_floor = np.full((200, 200), 2.0, dtype=np.float32)\n+    np.savez(\n+        floor,\n+        origin=np.array([-1.0, -5.0]),\n+        cell=0.05,\n+        floor_height=-1.25,\n+        up=np.array([0.0, -1.0, 0.0]),\n+        axes=np.array([0, 2]),\n+        free=open_floor > 0,\n+        clearance=open_floor,\n+        clearance_low=open_floor,\n+    )\n+    path = tmp_path / \"assets.json\"\n+    path.write_text(json.dumps({\"scene_id\": \"t\", \"assets\": [box(\"far\", [7, 1, 0], \"fixed\")]}))\n+    client = TestClient(create_app(path, floor))\n+    body = client.post(\"/api/route\", json={\"start\": [0, 1.25, 0], \"object_id\": \"far\"}).json()\n+    assert body[\"placeholder\"] is False\n+    assert body[\"path\"][0][1] == 1.25\n+\n+\n def test_move_updates_box_and_is_logged(client):\n     moved = {\"op\": \"move\", \"object_id\": \"near\", \"position\": [5, 1, 0]}\n     assert client.post(\"/api/changes\", json=moved).status_code == 200\n====HEAD\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/route\")\n    def route(request: RouteRequest) -> dict:\n        asset = require(request.object_id)\n        if grid is not None:\n            try:\n                found = plan_route(\n                    grid,\n                    tuple(request.start),\n                    tuple(asset[\"bbox_min\"]),\n                    tuple(asset[\"bbox_max\"]),\n                    width=PROFILES[request.profile],\n                    footprints=footprints(store, request.object_id),\n                )\n            except NoRoute as reason:\n                raise HTTPException(409, str(reason)) from None\n            return {\n                \"path\": found.path,\n                \"length\": round(found.length, 3),\n                \"stop_distance\": round(found.stop_distance, 3),\n                \"view_from\": list(found.view_from),\n                \"profile\": request.profile,\n                \"width\": PROFILES[request.profile],\n                \"placeholder\": False,\n            }\n        floor_y = store.scene.get(\"floor_y\", request.start[1])\n        path, length = placeholder_route(tuple(request.start), tuple(asset[\"center\"]), floor_y)\n        return {\n            \"path\": path,\n            \"length\": round(length, 3),\n            \"profile\": request.profile,\n            \"width\": PROFILES[request.profile],\n            \"placeholder\": True,\n        }\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/copilot/query\")\n12:def room():\n26:def cells_of(route):\n30:def crosses_wall(route, grid=GRID):\n40:def test_route_goes_through_the_gap_and_not_the_wall():\n47:def test_route_stays_on_the_floor_and_stops_close_to_the_target():\n53:def test_too_wide_a_body_gets_a_reason_instead_of_a_route():\n58:def test_footprint_in_the_gap_blocks_then_moving_it_reopens_the_route():\n66:def test_start_inside_an_obstacle_snaps_to_nearby_floor():\n71:def test_start_far_from_any_floor_is_refused():\n76:def test_line_check_sees_blocked_cells():\n83:def test_viewing_point_stands_back_from_the_target_along_the_route():\n# eduard-rednic: eduard\n**Goal:** floor, routing, nearby search and backend API (`app/nav/`, `app/api/`), per docs/PLAN.md.\n**Done:** `make api` on port 8001. PR #1 merged. PR #2 adds real A* with body sizes in `/api/route`, used when `NAV_GRID` or the default `nav_grid.npz` exists; otherwise the marked placeholder.\n**Verified:** `make check` passes. A* takes under 20 ms on the real map. Not yet run against real objects; floor not checked against views.\n**Next:** load `assets_final.json`, pick a reachable `P-005`; object footprints for moves; TimescaleDB.\n**Decided:** no cloud: TimescaleDB runs on the local 5090, and tablets talk only to it.\n**Blockers:** `assets_final.json` and the `P-005` choice from Viktor; Hannu's code isn't on main and his fixture format differs.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"42483fb1-2ebb-47a3-b37e-5814f1bde146","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","branch":"viktor/viewer-objects","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":6,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":null,"remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf420953-526b-4a53-9735-c6f971077178","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/viewer-objects","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
