{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01W2z6u48mE7ruGEe22DNPVT","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"eb1ff47f-cfbf-49b1-a15e-4ca693f2c22a","ownerOrganizationUuid":"af454b37-7570-4ffb-9890-36a908611f8b"}
{"parentUuid":"916a8f5d-0438-421c-88ef-865ca816a2f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgnq9MJTkU7B2kjFZUeVj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1602,"cache_read_input_tokens":204332,"output_tokens":1700,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":620},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1602,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1700,"cache_read_input_tokens":204332,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1602},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":15257,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"d40c0cf9-c777-4ebb-89bd-b671476051a0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgnq9M45aDzSgvaSWoxdd","requestRef":"ab0ba625-5a91-4417-8436-14658fe793a8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"bcf4a312-b2ec-4188-8500-8a707122375e","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:08:13.697Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/scene-full","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"bcf4a312-b2ec-4188-8500-8a707122375e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgnq9MJTkU7B2kjFZUeVj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**It's probably not mainly the GPU.** A weak GPU mostly lowers the frame rate, though Spark can also draw fewer splats on a weaker device. I haven't seen your screen, but from the code and files there are three likelier causes, roughly from easiest to hardest to fix.\n\n**1. The viewer's speed settings soften the image**\n- **Level of detail is on by default:** Spark draws far areas with fewer, bigger splats, and how many it draws depends on the device. That's the one way the GPU can affect the look.\n- **Resolution is fixed at 1 pixel per CSS pixel:** on a high-DPI screen or tablet, that looks blurry.\n\n**2. The light file has lost some colour information**\n- `light_full.ply` has every splat, but only their base colour. Shine and other changes in colour with viewing angle are gone. On the old scene, that scored 28.6 dB against a full render, which looks close but not identical.\n- `clean.ply` keeps that colour information.\n\n**3. The splat itself is only good near where the video was filmed**\n- **Holes and floaters:** the black holes, floating blobs and smears are part of the scene, so no GPU will fix them.\n- **Distance from the filming path:** my own renders of `clean.ply` showed this clearly. The pump looks good from 1.6–2 m and is a mess from about 1.2 m.\n- **Eye height:** the viewer's eye is at 1.6 m, but the camera filmed at about 1.33 m, so walk mode always sits above the path the scene was trained on. It's a quick fix that should help.\n\n**To find out which it is,** run this on the 5090, then open the viewer with `?lod=0&res=2` on the end of the URL:\n```\nmake web SCENE=data/scene/splat_v2/clean.ply ASSETS=data/scene/splat_v2/assets_viewer.json SHAPES=data/scene/splat_v2/shapes.json\n```\nThen compare what you see near the pumps with my reference render, which also uses `clean.ply`, on a server GPU:\n`/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad/floor_v2/arrive.jpg`\n\n| What you see | Cause | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| It now looks like my render | Viewer settings or the light file | Change the defaults and use `clean.ply` on the 5090. The tablet will need a lighter version |\n| It's still worse than my render | Spark and gsplat draw the scene differently | I'd need to look into Spark's settings |\n| It looks like my render, but that's still not good enough | The splat itself | Remove floaters, lower the eye height, and keep the demo camera near the filmed path |\n\nWhich file were you viewing, and on which machine? If it was `make web` with no `SCENE=`, you were seeing the sample scene. This ThinkPad has no NVIDIA GPU, so it isn't a fair test either.\n\nWhatever the result, I'd make two changes: set the eye height to about 1.33 m and remove floaters from the viewer scene. Do you want me to go ahead? The eye height is in Benjamin's viewer code, but it's only a one-line change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1602,"cache_read_input_tokens":204332,"output_tokens":1700,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":620},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1602,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1700,"cache_read_input_tokens":204332,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1602},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d40c0cf9-c777-4ebb-89bd-b671476051a0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"re