{"parentUuid":"7ff48891-1cd6-4a80-aca5-87a62971b096","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnqJw4UJTDBdc1DzNQTm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3991,"cache_read_input_tokens":205934,"output_tokens":2023,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1185},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3991,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2023,"cache_read_input_tokens":205934,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3991},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13737,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"788f6544-8e38-4f7a-86e2-fc27e05a2730","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgnqJupJn3ohmYouVLK1j","requestRef":"f2c71d53-48fc-45c6-8fa9-637f8822f40e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"96649237-9cb5-45c0-94d4-9c249de41829","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:10:22.106Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/scene-full","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"96649237-9cb5-45c0-94d4-9c249de41829","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnqJw4UJTDBdc1DzNQTm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**It's not the GPU.** The counter at the top seems to show 121 FPS with the pixel ratio at 2.0, on `clean.ply`, so the GPU is keeping up easily. This also isn't our viewer, it's a different splat viewer, which rules out Spark and our settings for what you see here. What's left is the splat itself.\n\nThings in the middle distance actually look good: the door, pipes, cart, washing machine and ladder are all readable. The bad parts are specific:\n\n| What you see | Likely cause | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Black holes in the floor** | The camera stayed about 1.33 m up and rarely looked straight down, so parts of the floor have few or no splats. The viewer's black background then shows through | Fill the holes with floor-coloured splats, and use a less harsh background |\n| **Blurry blobs close to the camera** (bottom of the image) | Floaters, plus areas seen by very few frames, which show up large when you're near them | Remove floaters at all heights, drop oversized splats, and keep the demo camera near the filmed path |\n| **Spiky, streaky edges** (floor, ceiling, right side) | Standard 3DGS training lets splats stretch into long needles wherever few frames constrain them | Retrain with a penalty on stretched splats |\n\n**What I'd do, in order:**\n1. **Clean up a copy for viewing (about 30 minutes):** remove floaters and oversized splats, fill the floor holes, and change the background. Objects and labels stay tied to the current `clean.ply`, so nothing else needs re-running. This should fix the most obvious problems.\n2. **Set the eye height to about 1.33 m and start the demo camera on the filmed path:** this is a small viewer change, so I'd let Benjamin know.\n3. **Retrain only if it's still not good enough (optional):** use all 1,496 frames, up from 1,179, with the stretch penalty. Training took about 25 minutes last time, but objects, labels and the floor map would all need re-running, and a retrain might not help. If we do it, it has to happen before your Roihu cert expires at 20:41.\n\nThe filled floor would be invented visual data, not something scanned. It's only cosmetic and doesn't affect objects or routing, but we should say so in the technical note, and the floor map won't use it.\n\nShall I start on step 1? I'd compare before and after from this same viewpoint and check that the pump view hasn't got worse. If you click **Copy State** in that viewer and paste it here, I can try to match your exact camera."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3991,"cache_read_input_tokens":205934,"output_tokens":2023,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1185},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3991,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2023,"cache_read_input_tokens":205934,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3991},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"788f6544-8e38-4f7a-86e2-fc27e05a2730","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgnqJupJn3ohmYouVLK1j","requestRef":"f2c71d53-48fc-45c6-8fa9-637f8822f40e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"f9600f52-a45c-4222-ab4b-f2cebaa7ecef","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:10:30.477Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"62939