{"parentUuid":"370c04b4-6c96-430b-83c5-a28fdb66406b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnqsdYguUJUEtYAPAsFN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016XYWCqrfoJmQyVZFHJzttM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; cat > handoffs/viktortrilar.md <<'EOF'\n# viktortrilar: viktor/scene-look\n**Goal:** fix how the scene looks in the viewer, and find out why Valmet's splat looks so different\n**Done:** app/scene/tidy.py (viewer copy: removes floaters and oversized splats, fills floor holes with made-up flat splats); train_splat.py gains `--max-stretch` and `--seed-points`; viewer eye height 1.33 m. All uncommitted so far\n**Verified:** lint passes; new tidy and stretch tests pass or skip without torch. Same-viewpoint renders: Valmet's splat is far more complete than ours away from the filmed path. Valmet has no needle splats (capped near 10:1), ours 16%. Our 26.57 vs 11.82 dB comparison may be unfair to Valmet: its scene has a chair not seen in ours, so it may be a different capture (not confirmed). Our video is real handheld footage\n**Roihu:** retrain job 2926105 (`runs/splat_v2b`), then comparison job writing `runs/floor_v2/compare_all.jpg`. Cleaned current scene: `data/scene/splat_v2/tidy.ply`. Cert valid to 2026-11-07 20:41\n**Next:** look at compare_all.jpg, then Viktor decides which scene to demo. Returning to Valmet's means lift_v1 objects (441, AI-reviewed labels) and a new P-005 pick. Update docs/RESULTS.md, which still says own splat is clearly better\n**Blockers:** none. P-005 on obj-0048 is still an unconfirmed pick, on the own-splat objects only\nEOF\ngit add handoffs/viktortrilar.md app/scene/tidy.py app/scene/train_splat.py tests/test_scene_tidy.py tests/test_train_splat.py web/main.js; git commit -qm \"Add a viewer cleanup tool and splat training options, and lower the eye height\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git l