{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01W2z6u48mE7ruGEe22DNPVT","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"eb1ff47f-cfbf-49b1-a15e-4ca693f2c22a","ownerOrganizationUuid":"af454b37-7570-4ffb-9890-36a908611f8b"}
{"parentUuid":"86249398-f845-4f6e-8c51-574753542b79","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnrpB9DnmBaFNqfyKA57","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_read_input_tokens":249432,"output_tokens":1129,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":401},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":249432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4104,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"da539a9d-4cc6-4e23-b5a5-348b39a5f60d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgnrpAeTWtv9neEf3PUqw","requestRef":"56b2d7ee-f61a-446f-976e-6dd1644d9f69","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"022c8fb8-5dd8-4a2d-8169-41fd93e78fe1","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:29:56.028Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/scene-look","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"022c8fb8-5dd8-4a2d-8169-41fd93e78fe1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnrpB9DnmBaFNqfyKA57","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Because the test was set up in a way that favoured our splat, and that's my mistake.** It answered \"which scene best reproduces our own video?\", not \"which scene looks better when you walk around it?\".\n\n1. **It tested close to our training data.** The 40 test frames came from the same video our splat was trained on. Held-out frames sit right next to training frames, so our splat barely had to predict anything new. It looks great on the filmed path and falls apart about 0.6 m off it, and the test never left that path.\n2. **The test camera almost never looked where ours is weak.** The video stays about 1.33 m up and rarely looks straight down, so it mostly missed the floor holes and the ceiling.\n3. **Valmet's splat had to pass through an alignment first.** I fitted it to our coordinates with ICP. PSNR punishes even small shifts heavily, so a few centimetres of error scores badly on detailed scenes like pipes and brick.\n4. **Valmet's score was suspiciously low.** 11.82 dB is roughly what you'd expect from badly mismatched images, and that should have made me stop and check. I noted in `docs/RESULTS.md` that alignment \"may lower its score\", but I still treated the result as a win.\n5. **The two scenes may differ in content.** Valmet's has a chair I haven't seen in ours, and it's brighter overall (average colour about 0.62 vs 0.49 in red). If lighting or objects differ, the score drops even for a perfect splat.\n\nI also called ours \"clearly better by eye\", but I only looked at those same on-path views. The first time I rendered both from new viewpoints was today, and the result reversed.\n\n**How much each cause counted is still unmeasured.** The queued job would show this by rendering Valmet's splat from our real camera poses next to the actual frames. If it's misaligned, you'd see the two images offset.\n\n**The comparison I should have run** has no training-data advantage: fixed viewpoints away from both filmed paths, including looking down, judged on holes and completeness. On that side-by-side, Valmet's looks clearly better.\n\nYour decision to switch rested on my result, so it's worth revisiting. Once the retrain and comparison finish, I'll recommend which scene to demo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_read_input_tokens":249432,"output_tokens":1129,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":401},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":249432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"da539a9d-4cc6-4e23-b5a5-348b39a5f60d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgnrpAeTWtv9neEf3PUqw","requestRef":"56b2d7ee-f61a-446f-976e-6dd1644d9f69","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ddeeb880-e14c-46bb-989b-fa0de1ecab55","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:30:03.877Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/scene-look","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
