{"parentUuid":"08d3971a-a332-4feb-826e-1ec88d8f940e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgns4gzyqqMfGzWrKhuk8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Yes, everything is still there, and the labels are actually better than on our splat.**\n\n| What | Where | Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| Segmentation masks | Roihu `data/vlsplat_all` | All 700 views, with masks, JSON and overlay images |\n| Rendered views and depth | Roihu `data/scene/equipment_room/render`, `render_detail` | 400 + 300 views |\n| Valmet's cleaned scene | Roihu `data/scene/equipment_room/clean.ply` | 1,178,554 splats |\n| 3D objects | Roihu `runs/lift_v1` | 441 objects, plus `object_masks.json` and `splat_labels.npy` (its size matches the splat count) |\n| Labels | Roihu `runs/lift_v1` | Qwen labels and my AI review |\n| Fitted shapes | Local scratchpad `lift_v1/shapes.json` | Not in Roihu's `lift_v1`. Should also be in the `objects-v1` Release, but my check of that archive's contents didn't complete |\n| Team download | Release `objects-v1` (94 MB) | Has no `make` command yet |\n\n**How the two sets compare:**\n\n| | Valmet's scene (`lift_v1`) | Our splat (`lift_v2`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Objects | 441 | 574 |\n| Splats in objects | 306,360 (26%) | 907,742 (42%) |\n| Well-labelled | 362 AI-reviewed, 16 likely | 0 AI-reviewed, 113 likely |\n| Unsure or unknown | 63 | 461 |\n| Mobility | 232 fixed, 52 movable, 157 unsure | 93 fixed, 19 movable, 462 unsure |\n\nThe AI review is my own visual check, not verified by a person, but it's still a big head start.\n\n**What going back would need:**\n- **Floor map:** there isn't one on Roihu for this scene. Rebuilding should be quick, and carving can use the existing renders. Route results may differ from the earlier 7.4 m².\n- **P-005:** it needs a new pick. The current one, obj-0048, only exists in our splat's objects. The earlier by-eye candidates in Valmet's scene were obj-0046, 0100, 0109 and 0155, and I'd check whether the two inline pumps are visible there too.\n- **Downloads:** a `make` command for Valmet's scene and its objects.\n- **Eduard, Benjamin and anyone else using `make scene`:** they'd need to switch, because object IDs differ between the two sets.\n\nThe comparison job is still running, but this makes going back to Valmet's scene cheap. It would mean no re-running of the segmentation. Do you want me to wait for the comparison, or start on this now?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1301,"cache_read_input_tokens":251455,"output_tokens":1118,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":190},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1301,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1118,"cache_read_input_tokens":251455,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1301},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"10fe8746-11e6-4c18-87a7-71223edc4c37","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgns4gj7Tieq3KS2ce7yv","requestRef":"b3175eae-f149-4172-a956-b568a86f43f3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"5aaa7a7e-8f42-4066-97e1-11577b96562e","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:33:19.019Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/scene-look","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
