{"parentUuid":"e51cce41-58dc-45d1-87b4-3018be7ec47b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnsCWeMN1jNzm4xHXAEr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_read_input_tokens":252756,"output_tokens":1452,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":467},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":252756,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5431,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"fef21e2f-b7a2-4a43-a9fc-b0f47ec30b99","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgnsCWK1S5wNH8WJuP7A7","requestRef":"000ad869-c6d8-4419-a382-ba290663e38b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"3255cfe1-5ab9-44a5-9046-365ec3024c14","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:35:00.358Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/scene-look","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"3255cfe1-5ab9-44a5-9046-365ec3024c14","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnsCWeMN1jNzm4xHXAEr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The biggest improvement is to demo on Valmet's scene and use our video for what it's best at: sharp, real close-ups.** That gives us the better-looking room plus detail Valmet's splat can't match. It's my recommendation unless the comparison job surprises me.\n\nIn score order:\n\n**1. Asset extraction (30%)**\n- **Label from real video frames, not renders.** We have 1,496 sharp 1080p frames, and the objects can be projected into them if the alignment holds up. This is likely the biggest label gain, especially for pumps and valves.\n- **Try to read tags and nameplates in those frames.** A readable tag would be real evidence for P-005 and other assets, which is what \"never invent identity\" asks for. I don't know yet whether any are legible.\n- **Cover more of the scene.** Only 26% of Valmet's splats belong to an object, against 42% on ours. More views from its complete floor and upper areas should raise that.\n- **Clean up the objects.** Merge split tank pieces and group pipes into runs, so the object list makes sense to someone reading it.\n\n**2. Navigation (25%)**\n- **Draw routes in the viewer.** It's still the biggest visible gap.\n- **Rebuild the floor map on Valmet's scene,** using carving and our walked path. That depends on the same alignment check.\n- **Show a live re-route:** move a cart, and the route changes. The API handles this, but the viewer doesn't send moves to it yet, and it's directly what Valmet's engineer said would earn extra credit.\n\n**3. AI diagnostics (20%)**\n- **Run the real P-005 question through Hannu and Eduard's copilot,** checking that its answer cites the actual records: the FOULING events, the motor current rising from 41.4 to 48.8 A, and the bearing temperature trend.\n- **Confirm which pump is P-005** with Valmet's engineer.\n\n**4. Backend and demo (25%)**\n- **Rehearse the full flow** on the 5090 and a tablet with no internet. None of this has been tested as one flow.\n- **Choose a safe camera path.** Check how far Valmet's scene holds up off its path, and keep the demo inside that.\n- **Write one clear scene comparison** for the slides, using fixed viewpoints, and correct `docs/RESULTS.md`.\n\n**What I'd stop doing:** more retraining of our own splat. It can't fill in views the video never captured, like the floor directly below. The running job will still show how far it gets, but I wouldn't spend more time on it unless the result is striking.\n\n**Suggested order:**\n1. Check the alignment. Nearly everything above that uses our video depends on it.\n2. Switch back to Valmet's scene, with a new floor map, P-005 pick and `make` command.\n3. Relabel from real frames.\n4. Benjamin or I add route drawing while that runs.\n\nShould I start on step 1 now? It needs the queued job, or a smaller check if you'd rather not use the GPU."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_read_input_tokens":252756,"output_tokens":1452,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":467},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":252756,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fef21e2f-b7a2-4a43-a9fc-b0f47ec30b99","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgnsCWK1S5wNH8WJuP7A7","requestRef":"000ad869-c6d8-4419-a382-ba290663e38