{"parentUuid":"aec3635d-99af-41a8-b992-cd52fccb7723","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgnt4yBS85jmYw76bG4QR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**I don't have that answer yet, but the job rendering it is running now.** It shows Valmet's uncleaned splat, our uncleaned splat and our stretch-limited retrain side by side, from the same viewpoints, including looking down and 0.6 m off the path.\n\n**What I can say so far:**\n- **On our video's own viewpoints:** our uncleaned splat looks very close to the real frames, with a full floor and door. Its score was 22.31 dB on 40 held-out frames, against 17.48 dB after cleaning.\n- **Valmet's uncleaned version:** I haven't looked at it yet. Every Valmet render so far used the cleaned copy, and it still looked good despite that damage, with some black patches on the door and walls. Uncleaned, it may well look better still.\n- **A score won't settle this.** Valmet's splat is a different capture from our video, with different objects and floor, so it can't score fairly against our frames. Off-path renders judged by eye are the fair test, and neither scene has a score advantage there.\n\nMy expectation, not a result: ours may be sharper near the filmed path, and Valmet's more complete away from it, especially at the ceiling. The camera rarely looked up in our video.\n\nI'll bring you the side-by-side and a recommendation as soon as it's done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1872,"cache_read_input_tokens":282202,"output_tokens":422,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1872,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":2822