{"parentUuid":"1b6be801-5213-4439-b81b-728757b43385","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgntENeKKMLXtiTgs2u3M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WWdzJuo16S4pn9aMmUXAjV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; make lint 2>&1 | grep -v VIRTUAL | tail -14 | cut -c1-120; git status --short | cut -c1-60; cat > handoffs/viktortrilar.md <<'EOF'\n# viktortrilar: viktor/keep-faint-splats\n**Goal:** demo on Valmet's original `Equipment Room.ply`, with objects built from undamaged renders\n**Done:** found that `clean_mask` (opacity above 0.05) removed 30% of splats and caused the black holes, in both scenes. Default is now 0.001. Corrected docs/RESULTS.md: the 26.57 vs 11.82 dB result is retracted, as Valmet's scene is a different capture\n**Verified:** app/scene/load.py tests pass. Own splat on 40 frames: 22.31 dB uncleaned, 17.48 dB with the old cleaning. Uncleaned Valmet looks near-photographic by eye from every viewpoint tried\n**Roihu:** pipeline job 2926409 on the original: `data/scene/valmet_full`, `data/masks_v3`, `runs/lift_v3`. Default test job 2926421. Original at `data/scene/equipment_room/original.ply`. Cert valid to 2026-11-07 20:41\n**Next:** compare lift_v3 with objects-v1, and agree with Eduard before replacing it, because object IDs and `assets_mapped.json` change. Then pick P-005 again, label from real frames, and publish with a make target. Viewer should load the uncleaned original, not `light_full.ply`\n**Blockers:** none. Open: which pump is P-005 (obj-0046 is a test pick). Floor map assumes our walked path carries over to Valmet's scene, where objects differ\nEOF","description":"See the lint failure and update the handoff","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4060,"cache_read_input_tokens":299189,"output_tokens":794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":52},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4060,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":299189,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4060},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":5786,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WWdzJuo16S4pn9aMmUXAjV":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; make lint 2>&1 | grep -v VIRTUAL | tail -14 | cut -c1-120; git status --short | cut -c1-60; cat > handoffs/viktortrilar.md <<'EOF'\n# viktortrilar: viktor/keep-faint-splats\n**Goal:** demo on Valmet's original `Equipment Room.ply`, with objects built from undamaged renders\n**Done:** found that `clean_mask` (opacity above 0.05) removed 30% of splats and caused the black holes, in both scenes. Default is now 0.001. Corrected docs/RESULTS.md: the 26.57 vs 11.82 dB result is retracted, as Valmet's scene is a different capture\n**Verified:** app/scene/load.py tests pass. Own splat on 40 frames: 22.31 dB uncleaned, 17.48 dB with the old cleaning. Uncleaned Valmet looks near-photographic by eye from every viewpoint tried\n**Roihu:** pipeline job 2926409 on the original: `data/scene/valmet_full`, `data/masks_v3`, `runs/lift_v3`. Default test job 2926421. Original at `data/scene/equipment_room/original.ply`. Cert valid to 2026-11-07 20:41\n**Next:** compare lift_v3 with objects-v1, and agree with Eduard before replacing it, because object IDs and `assets_mapped.json` change. Then pick P-005 again, label from real frames, and publish with a make target. Viewer should load the uncleaned original, not `light_full.ply`\n**Blockers:** none. Open: which pump is P-005 (obj-0046 is a test pick). Floor map assumes our walked path carries over to Valmet's scene, where objects differ\nEOF","description":"See the lint failure and update the handoff","timeout":60000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"35aae2b7-72dc-4084-b160-2e1943ff7f9f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgntENJjAzzLd1oEFFTDD","requestRef":"851f624e-4aa5-4ab7-9b79-c128db5eb1be","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"79bcf01f-5c84-4046-9ce3-f0e2f6a62f6c","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:48:33.768Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/keep-faint-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
