{"parentUuid":"f7aaf91f-3cdc-4290-abdc-0b6aa38870b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgntG9U74GfeWfrpuWhAh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":616,"cache_read_input_tokens":304336,"output_tokens":1089,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":616,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1089,"cache_read_input_tokens":304336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":616},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9320,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"f479ab6d-8057-4c98-be3d-0d28d6feb582","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgntG963KV3uVujFFsZEx","requestRef":"006fc089-864c-452a-b5b7-8465610ee224","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"092403b1-f928-41b3-8952-871bcf3bbdaa","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:49:00.314Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/keep-faint-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"092403b1-f928-41b3-8952-871bcf3bbdaa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgntG9U74GfeWfrpuWhAh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Yes, Valmet's is the better scene, so that's what we should demo.** It holds up from every viewpoint I rendered, while ours has smeared walls and no real ceiling. Eduard had also already switched `main` to it in PR #9. Side-by-side: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad/floor_v2/raw_all_small.jpg`\n\n| | Valmet's, uncleaned | Ours, uncleaned |\n|---|---|---|\n| Overall look | Near-photographic | Readable near our path, smeared elsewhere |\n| Floor and ceiling | Complete | Floor mostly complete, ceiling broken |\n| Fine detail | Sharp | Decent on the path, weak off it |\n\nThe stretch-limited retrain removed the needles, but looks no better by eye. I've dropped that and the floor-filling tool.\n\n**My cleaning damaged everything built so far.** It removed 30% of the splats in both scenes, so everything built on it, including `objects-v1`, came from renders with black holes in them. That includes Eduard's current setup.\n\n**To see the good version now:**\n```\nmake web SCENE=\"Equipment Room.ply\"\n```\nIt's about 415 MB, so judge it on the 5090. The `light_full.ply` and `light_400k.ply` in `objects-v1` were made from the damaged scene, so they'll look worse, and the tablet will need a new light version.\n\n**Running or done:**\n- **Pipeline on Valmet's original (job 2926409):** new renders, masks, objects, labels, shapes and floor map, in separate folders so nothing existing changes. It's on the masks step, and the last full run took about 30 minutes.\n- **Cleaning fix:** the default threshold is now effectively off, with a test added. A job is measuring whether that alone removes the damage, because the cleaning has other filters I haven't ruled out.\n- **Results correction:** `docs/RESULTS.md` now retracts my 26.57 vs 11.82 dB comparison.\n- **Commit:** `7a190fc` on `viktor/keep-faint-splats`, local only for now. Lint passes, and so do the tests (109 passed, 18 skipped).\n\n**Still open:**\n- **Replacing `objects-v1`:** new objects mean new IDs, which breaks Eduard's mapping of the 30 Excel records. I'll compare the results first, and only replace them if they're clearly better. Please let Eduard know this is coming.\n- **Floor map:** it uses our video's walked path, but Valmet's capture has different movable objects, such as the chair. That path may run through something in Valmet's scene, so I'll check.\n- **P-005:** it needs picking again on the new objects, and a person still has to confirm it.\n\nI'll report the comparison as soon as the pipeline finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":616,"cache_read_input_tokens":304336,"output_tokens":1089,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":616,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1089,"cache_read_input_tokens":304336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":616},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f479ab6d-8057-4c98-be3d-0d28d6feb582","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgntG963KV3uVujFFsZEx","requestRef":"006fc089-864c-452a-b5b7-8465610ee224","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"257a0017-161e-4afd-8f04-addfd5ea3d8b","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:49:02.126Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","user